          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Humanitarian AI agents deployed by IRC provide critical assistance to refugees as crises outpace capacity",
            "articleSection": "Daily Utility",
            "abstract": "The International Rescue Committee has deployed purpose-built AI agents to provide information and assistance to refugees and displaced populations, as humanitarian organisations face caseloads that vastly exceed human staff capacity. The AI system is designed with a safety-first architecture, aiming to avoid the harms that general-purpose AI tools can cause in high-stakes, vulnerable-population contexts. The deployment represents one of the most significant real-world tests of AI in the humanitarian sector to date.",
            "url": "https://restofworld.org/2026/irc-signpost-humanitarian-ai-refugee-assistance/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=feeds",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
